    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions of the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in at night or in reduced visibility.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway clear of overhanging branches to allow passage of fire apparatus and ambulances.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the driveway to maintain a clear line of sight from the road to the residence.\n• Keep the circular driveway fully passable and free of parked vehicles so arriving apparatus can pull through without reversing.\n• Designate a staging area on the circular driveway where a second arriving unit can position without blocking the primary access route.\n• Thin dense vegetation bordering the driveway to reduce conditions that could slow or stop responder access if fire moves onto the property.\n• Keep the circular driveway surface in a condition that supports the weight of heavy emergency vehicles year-round.\n• Post a clearly visible address sign at the residence itself so responders arriving on scene can confirm they have reached the correct structure.\n• Identify and mark any secondary path across open terrain that could serve as an alternate way out if the main driveway becomes blocked."
