    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or touching the house on all sides.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to open up space between tree canopies and the roofline.\n• Remove shrubs growing beneath tree canopies close to the house so fire cannot climb from ground level into the trees.\n• Clear a wider gap between the nearest shrub clusters and the walls of the structure.\n• Cut back any shrubs or low branches that overhang or lean toward the house.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Widen any narrow sections of the driveway where vegetation has grown inward from the sides.\n• Clear a turnaround area at or near the end of the driveway large enough for a fire truck to reverse direction.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible to emergency responders approaching from the road.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from shrubs growing near the structure.\n• Maintain the open green space near the house by keeping grass cut short and removing any dead growth.\n• Thin shrub clusters on the uphill or windward sides of the house before addressing lower-priority sides.\n• Keep a clear, unobstructed path around all sides of the structure for firefighter movement."
